description:
Goal: Create an operationally deterministic procedure and automation suite for coordinating hotpatches, rollbacks, and customer communications when a model rollout causes regressions localized to canary slices or tenant cohorts across Hosted, Dedicated, and Private planes. This ticket covers:

- a deterministic handshake and gating protocol so a fix applied in one plane (e.g., Hosted) can be safely propagated or refused in Dedicated/Private;
- kv-cache reconciliation guidance and scripts to avoid sticky state after rollbacks;
- tenant-scoped patch orchestration (per-tenant rollbacks, prioritized fast-paths for top-tier customers);
- templated customer communication artifacts and a runbook for Solutions/Support to use during escalations;
- automation to lift metrics and synthesize a triage verdict (regression, noise, or non-deterministic) within the first 15 minutes of canary degradation;
- post-mortem checklist items to ensure lessons are codified into runtime and Console automation.

We will prioritize minimizing end-user downtime, avoiding cascading KV-cache inconsistencies, and ensuring customers in Dedicated/Private receive clear, compliant instructions when manual steps are required (e.g., private infra upgrades).
